Cataly - modified-copy notice and source attribution

Project: https://github.com/vntrevx/Cataly
Maintainer: vntrevx (https://github.com/vntrevx)

Cataly integrates messenger-facing ownership from dori-superagent, the native
oh-my-pi coding-agent runtime, and the outcome-driven workflows of omp-ulw.
The Cataly name identifies this maintained integration; it does not replace
the original authors' credit or the license attached to each source.

Source provenance
-----------------

This is a modified copy of sisyphuslabs/dori-superagent, based on
97d807b9037cb050a72129659cf6306d8055010d (2026-11-11 source snapshot).
It incorporates OMP-specific adaptations from omp-dori source
75a1b28de8caddb6d30b2e3d72ef3dec09450b47, with further changes for sessions,
goals, approvals, monitors, runtime adapters, configuration, packaging,
and documentation.

It also integrates upstream 49fba4dc081c9238f01e617b2fd17f548438e624 while
preserving the local adaptations and separately bound omp-ulw source.

The dori-superagent-derived material retains Sustainable Use License 1.0
and its notices in LICENSE. The pre-existing omp-dori material incorporated
from the local source, including its extension and OMP integration changes,
retains the MIT terms and YeonGyu Kim, betive37, and vntrevx notices in
LICENSE.omp-dori. Third-party components keep their own licenses. This
modified copy does not claim that upstream SUL material has become MIT.

Bound upstream sources
----------------------

This distribution includes modified-copy patch excerpts for:

- oh-my-pi (https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi), based on
  c308970263ae13744ea15ab67302e3dac840e266 / 18.20.0.
- omp-ulw (https://github.com/dbc-hbin/omp-ulw), based on
  33b375dc8d289d6fec944a8a5ee8f2db721a8c34.

native-omp.lock/native-omp.patch and omp-ulw.overlay.lock/omp-ulw.patch bind
those bases, patch digests, and resulting source identities. omp-ulw.lock
retains its upstream repository/commit meaning. These are prepared source
overlays, not a vendored union or an external fork dependency.

Original authors' copyright and license notices continue to apply to the
patch excerpts and fetched source. The default runtime uses the official,
version-matched MIT-licensed @oh-my-pi/pi-natives addon. Its compatibility
stamp does not establish a rebuilt binary or verify a source delta.

Private policy, provider settings, credentials, and QA workspace content
are not part of these source payloads. Installation and runtime activation
are separate actions: installing Cataly does not replace a running agent
or enable another harness, receiver, or service.

